WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:01:04.774
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
01:05.044 --> 01:08.649
Ma'am, can you please put up your seat?

3
01:09.316 --> 01:11.016
Thank you.

4
01:45.683 --> 01:48.716
[Welcome to Korea, Mantua]

5
02:07.849 --> 02:11.272
[Arrivals]

6
02:11.272 --> 02:13.116
Mr. Gong Eun Tae?

7
02:14.164 --> 02:15.644
Hello.

8
02:15.644 --> 02:19.183
I'm Martina, Head of Merchandising at Mantua.

9
02:20.100 --> 02:24.416
Oh, hello. I'm Gong Eun Tae from Hongsung Sales.

10
02:25.504 --> 02:29.268
Surprised to hear me speak Korean?

11
02:29.268 --> 02:32.844
Yes. I assumed you'd be Italian, of course.

12
02:32.844 --> 02:34.632
I am Italian.

13
02:34.632 --> 02:36.216
It's been a while since I was in Korea.

14
02:36.216 --> 02:37.376
Oh...

15
02:37.376 --> 02:39.483
Why did you come all the way to the airport?

16
02:39.483 --> 02:41.412
We could've met at the office.

17
02:41.412 --> 02:44.183
- Of course, I had to... - When you're overly welcoming,

18
02:44.183 --> 02:46.349
people can read your intentions, huh?

19
02:46.349 --> 02:49.183
How hard is what you're about to ask?

20
02:50.249 --> 02:51.820
Let's go.

21
02:51.820 --> 02:55.036
I can't wait to find out why you had me fly

22
02:55.036 --> 02:57.349
all the way to Korea.

23
03:04.983 --> 03:07.149
[The Ordinary Jackpot, Subtitle]

24
03:07.149 --> 03:13.096
[Episode 9, Interpreting the Past]

25
03:13.096 --> 03:15.420
Mr. Yang, about Mantua,

26
03:15.420 --> 03:18.849
their ownership structure is complicated, and they're all privately owned.

27
03:18.849 --> 03:21.383
There's no way they don't have any accounting records.

28
03:21.383 --> 03:24.284
What about that Martina? Did you look into her background?

29
03:24.284 --> 03:26.516
Well, about that...

30
03:28.004 --> 03:30.049
there's no data on her at all.

31
03:30.049 --> 03:31.049
How can there be nothing?

32
03:31.049 --> 03:33.016
Has she only worked at Mantua her whole life?

33
03:33.016 --> 03:34.583
It seems so.

34
03:34.583 --> 03:37.816
Darn it, who is this woman?

35
03:46.276 --> 03:48.549
Here's everything you ordered.

36
03:49.280 --> 03:51.383
- Thank you, sir. - Enjoy.

37
03:58.608 --> 04:01.516
[Risk & Mitigation Plan]

38
04:07.788 --> 04:10.816
The Chinese market...

39
04:10.816 --> 04:13.532
What do you think?

40
04:13.532 --> 04:15.792
Well...

41
04:15.792 --> 04:17.996
It's not bad, but...

42
04:17.996 --> 04:21.749
I doubt you made this move just for margins like these.

43
04:23.349 --> 04:26.383
CGM has entered the Korean market.

44
04:27.392 --> 04:29.940
You should've led with that.

45
04:29.940 --> 04:34.049
Wasn't CGM already in Korea as a vendor?

46
04:34.049 --> 04:38.883
They're setting up a Korean branch to control their brands directly.

47
04:38.883 --> 04:42.616
Of course, Korea isn't their only target.

48
04:42.616 --> 04:44.688
They want to use Korea as a logistics hub

49
04:44.688 --> 04:47.904
and enter China while avoiding tariffs.

50
04:47.904 --> 04:52.612
So Hongsung wants to enter China first with Mantua's backing?

51
04:52.612 --> 04:55.383
If Mantua enters China first,

52
04:55.383 --> 04:56.963
CGM won't be able to use its capital

53
04:56.963 --> 05:00.283
to pressure the Korean market as it does now.

54
05:14.344 --> 05:16.644
Is there coffee at the office?

55
05:16.644 --> 05:19.872
Well, we have a machine,

56
05:19.872 --> 05:21.749
but the temperature isn't quite right,

57
05:21.749 --> 05:24.649
so I brought this from a café I often go to.

58
05:25.408 --> 05:26.796
You know what?

59
05:26.796 --> 05:29.983
The soul of the person making it goes into the coffee.

60
05:36.849 --> 05:38.836
This person isn't a mere merchant.

61
05:38.836 --> 05:42.816
This coffee wasn't made for someone else.

62
05:49.104 --> 05:51.112
Mr. Gong,

63
05:51.112 --> 05:52.949
I don't want to fight CGM.

64
05:52.949 --> 05:56.356
They're not exactly clean players.

65
05:56.356 --> 06:01.583
Then you don't mind if CGM takes over the Chinese market?

66
06:02.284 --> 06:03.896
In the Bible,

67
06:03.896 --> 06:08.449
there's a parable about workers hired in the morning and evening.

68
06:08.449 --> 06:10.183
Have you heard of it?

69
06:10.183 --> 06:11.444
Oh, yes.

70
06:11.444 --> 06:15.949
The one where the owner pays two workers the same wage?

71
06:15.949 --> 06:17.849
Naturally, they'd complain.

72
06:17.849 --> 06:21.049
They worked different hours but got paid the same.

73
06:21.049 --> 06:24.884
When the morning workers complained, the owner said,

74
06:24.884 --> 06:29.440
"I gave you what I promised. Why are you complaining?"

75
06:29.440 --> 06:32.512
We're already doing the work we're given

76
06:32.512 --> 06:35.252
and getting what we're owed.

77
06:35.252 --> 06:38.649
Wherever CGM expands and however much they make

78
06:38.649 --> 06:41.384
has nothing to do with us.

79
06:41.384 --> 06:44.316
Then would you be fine

80
06:44.316 --> 06:48.749
if the evening workers took all the wages earned by the morning workers?

81
06:48.749 --> 06:53.016
More than 60 or 70% of Mantua's buyers are probably

82
06:53.016 --> 06:55.749
from Korea, China, Japan, and East Asia.

83
06:55.749 --> 06:58.504
And China likely makes up the largest share.

84
06:58.504 --> 07:01.808
If CGM sets up a warehouse in China,

85
07:01.808 --> 07:06.844
why would buyers in and around Guangzhou bother doing business with Mantua?

86
07:06.844 --> 07:08.648
If CGM enters China,

87
07:08.648 --> 07:13.883
Mantua won't just lose China, but the entire East Asian market.

88
07:15.183 --> 07:19.788
How much of our business do you think comes from retailers?

89
07:19.788 --> 07:22.976
That's not enough to justify going to war with CGM.

90
07:22.976 --> 07:25.549
The war has already begun.

91
07:25.549 --> 07:29.683
All we're asking is for Mantua to join the fight.

92
07:31.572 --> 07:34.648
I think I need some time to think.

93
07:34.648 --> 07:36.949
Of course. Take all the time you need.

94
07:36.949 --> 07:40.749
But could you give me a rough timeline?

95
07:40.749 --> 07:43.756
It won't take long. I'll decide while I'm in Korea.

96
07:43.756 --> 07:48.308
But I'd like someone to show me around while I'm here.

97
07:48.308 --> 07:51.404
It's been a while, so I'd like to look around.

98
07:51.404 --> 07:53.084
I'll show you around.

99
07:53.084 --> 07:55.828
No, assign your junior staff.

100
07:55.828 --> 07:57.683
If we end up working together,

101
07:57.683 --> 08:00.844
we'll be working mostly with Hongsung's junior staff, won't we?

102
08:00.844 --> 08:03.004
This is a long-term business.

103
08:03.004 --> 08:06.549
You two could get promoted into management and move on.

104
08:15.272 --> 08:18.028
Ji Hye, you'll have to handle the VIP reception.

105
08:18.028 --> 08:20.156
What? Me?

106
08:20.156 --> 08:23.720
I'll explain later. Just request a company car first.

107
08:23.720 --> 08:25.516
Oh, okay.

108
08:27.464 --> 08:28.616
Mr. Gong isn't going?

109
08:28.616 --> 08:29.816
Ugh, I don't know.

110
08:29.816 --> 08:31.872
That Martina woman is impossible to talk to.

111
08:31.872 --> 08:33.816
I can't tell what she's thinking.

112
08:44.149 --> 08:46.540
[Jung Sun Hyuk, Head of CGM Korea]

113
08:46.540 --> 08:48.240
Come in.

114
08:49.272 --> 08:50.972
Mr. Jung.

115
08:58.016 --> 09:00.283
[Team Leader Jung Sun Hyuk, Hongsung]

116
09:13.748 --> 09:15.216
Oh, dear.

117
09:15.216 --> 09:16.949
[Kim Soon Wook, Executive Director, Belmore Department Store]

118
09:17.812 --> 09:20.840
- Yes, Mr. Kim. - Sorry, I missed your call earlier.

119
09:20.840 --> 09:22.120
No problem at all.

120
09:22.120 --> 09:23.983
You called about the stores, right?

121
09:23.983 --> 09:27.932
Yes. I don't understand why the commission suddenly went up.

122
09:27.932 --> 09:30.249
I know. I just heard about it myself.

123
09:30.249 --> 09:32.528
It seems upper management decided to go that way.

124
09:32.528 --> 09:36.332
Mr. Kim, Hongsung pulled out instead of taking 20%, didn't they?

125
09:36.332 --> 09:38.316
Then you should keep it at 20% for us.

126
09:38.316 --> 09:41.536
With Hongsung out, we can't accept 22%.

127
09:41.536 --> 09:43.149
Oh, is that so?

128
09:43.149 --> 09:47.784
We agreed to go up to 22 if Hongsung took 20.

129
09:47.784 --> 09:50.640
Exactly. If Hongsung had taken it.

130
09:50.640 --> 09:53.088
Just consider it as they did.

131
09:53.088 --> 09:54.716
But, sir...

132
09:54.716 --> 09:57.312
No, wait... that's...

133
09:57.312 --> 09:58.908
- Mr. Jung. - Yes.

134
09:58.908 --> 10:02.160
Don't take this personally. Think about it.

135
10:02.160 --> 10:08.216
We gave up a stable partner like Hongsung to work with you, didn't we?

136
10:08.216 --> 10:09.649
This business may seem

137
10:09.649 --> 10:13.216
complicated, but it's pretty simple.

138
10:13.216 --> 10:15.316
We make the call because we think it'll work,

139
10:15.316 --> 10:16.856
and if you don't think it will,

140
10:16.856 --> 10:19.216
you can walk away.

141
10:19.216 --> 10:20.928
If you're walking away, say so now.

142
10:20.928 --> 10:23.049
Don't change your story later.

143
10:24.983 --> 10:27.796
Alright. We'll go with 22%.

144
10:27.796 --> 10:31.404
But I'd appreciate it if you could freeze the regular line.

145
10:31.404 --> 10:33.849
No, we can't.

146
10:33.849 --> 10:35.749
Keep it the same.

147
10:43.264 --> 10:46.128
Understood. Let's do that.

148
10:46.128 --> 10:48.549
Alright, bye.

149
10:56.500 --> 10:59.949
Darn it! Seriously!

150
11:05.244 --> 11:06.416
Team Leader Joo.

151
11:06.416 --> 11:07.416
Yes, sir.

152
11:07.416 --> 11:11.072
I need to find out what Hongsung is up to.

153
11:11.072 --> 11:14.316
Do you think Hongsung has another strategy?

154
11:14.316 --> 11:15.738
I think they're just

155
11:15.738 --> 11:19.416
planning to survive on the money they make from the penalties.

156
11:19.416 --> 11:20.680
No,

157
11:20.680 --> 11:22.864
Hongsung won't back down this easily.

158
11:22.864 --> 11:24.764
They've definitely got something.

159
11:24.764 --> 11:28.164
If we let Hongsung get the better of us now,

160
11:28.164 --> 11:29.508
we might as well shut everything down.

161
11:29.508 --> 11:31.316
You know what I mean?

162
11:31.316 --> 11:35.516
Find out exactly what Hongsung is thinking. Got it?

163
11:36.152 --> 11:38.783
Yes, sir.

164
11:58.349 --> 12:01.004
Hello, ma'am. I'm Lee Ji Hye.

165
12:01.004 --> 12:03.464
She'll be showing you around while you're in Korea.

166
12:03.464 --> 12:05.849
Her Italian is excellent too.

167
12:20.588 --> 12:22.288
Let's go.

168
12:33.349 --> 12:35.249
Call me right away if there's any problem.

169
12:35.249 --> 12:36.700
I'll be standing by.

170
12:36.700 --> 12:38.583
Yes, Mr. Gong.

171
12:58.716 --> 13:00.783
[Sungnyemun Gate]

172
13:07.549 --> 13:10.904
There's somewhere I'd like to stop by. Is that okay?

173
13:10.904 --> 13:13.568
Sure. Where would you like to go?

174
13:13.568 --> 13:17.183
I'm curious where you bought the clothes you're wearing.

175
13:17.900 --> 13:19.983
My outfit?

176
13:24.549 --> 13:27.383
[Hongin Intersection]

177
13:44.444 --> 13:46.424
There's no price tag?

178
13:46.424 --> 13:48.772
Excuse me, how much is this?

179
13:48.772 --> 13:51.620
Just give me 50,000 won.

180
13:51.620 --> 13:54.283
Don't tell anyone else.

181
13:54.283 --> 13:57.049
50,000 won... that's 30 euros.

182
13:57.712 --> 14:00.972
You bought those clothes here?

183
14:00.972 --> 14:03.349
Yes. They have all kinds of clothes here.

184
14:03.349 --> 14:07.183
Whenever fashion shows opened in Milan, Paris, London, or New York,

185
14:07.183 --> 14:09.983
identical pieces would appear here the next day.

186
14:09.983 --> 14:13.460
If they didn't sell in three days, they'd be thrown out.

187
14:13.460 --> 14:15.472
It's fallen off quite a bit since then,

188
14:15.472 --> 14:20.136
but it's still one of the best places in the world for the latest trends.

189
14:20.136 --> 14:22.883
If that were still true, it wouldn't have declined.

190
14:27.052 --> 14:31.516
Is there another reason you shop here besides the price?

191
14:32.704 --> 14:36.449
This is where I fell in love with clothes.

192
14:36.449 --> 14:41.583
Maybe this is also what made me want to work for Hongsung.

193
14:41.583 --> 14:44.949
You know that the same design doesn't mean the same clothes, right?

194
14:44.949 --> 14:48.416
Details are everything in clothing.

195
14:49.583 --> 14:52.008
There are plenty of good clothes here too.

196
14:52.008 --> 14:56.083
Even big brands often buy items from here just the way they are.

197
15:00.148 --> 15:03.583
So that's what you chose?

198
15:05.396 --> 15:08.183
You don't like my clothes?

199
15:09.480 --> 15:11.783
It's a 2022 summer Varnessa dress

200
15:11.783 --> 15:15.532
blended with a 2023 Marezi skirt design.

201
15:15.532 --> 15:19.216
The fabric is a Chinese cotton-polyester blend.

202
15:19.216 --> 15:23.216
It's been cut carelessly, without considering how the seams would line up.

203
15:23.216 --> 15:25.149
But let's put that aside.

204
15:25.783 --> 15:31.049
Do you even know how to care for different fabrics?

205
15:33.549 --> 15:35.983
Doctors aren't always healthy.

206
15:35.983 --> 15:38.216
People who sell alcohol don't need to be drinkers.

207
15:38.216 --> 15:40.649
But clothes are different.

208
15:40.649 --> 15:43.116
If you sell clothes,

209
15:43.116 --> 15:45.349
you should know clothes.

210
16:02.763 --> 16:04.996
- Mr. Gong. - Yes?

211
16:04.996 --> 16:07.496
Can I ask you something?

212
16:07.496 --> 16:09.828
You're going to ask anyway, right?

213
16:09.828 --> 16:12.060
Why did you send Ji Hye?

214
16:12.060 --> 16:13.804
Because she's the youngest.

215
16:13.804 --> 16:16.328
Martina specifically asked for a junior team member.

216
16:16.328 --> 16:18.516
You could've just made an excuse and sent Gi Tae.

217
16:18.516 --> 16:22.048
Martina doesn't know everyone on our team.

218
16:22.048 --> 16:25.028
And I thought Ji Hye would do a good job.

219
16:25.028 --> 16:28.849
How can someone like you be worrying this much?

220
16:30.316 --> 16:34.156
I'd be worried about anyone going, not just Ji Hye.

221
16:34.156 --> 16:35.396
Exactly.

222
16:35.396 --> 16:38.449
I'm worried that I can't focus on work either.

223
16:53.668 --> 16:54.788
- Mr. Yang. - Yeah?

224
16:54.788 --> 16:55.983
Looking for something?

225
16:55.983 --> 16:59.483
Well, I have a coffee I drink, but I can't find it.

226
17:04.449 --> 17:06.684
Don't bother. I'll do it.

227
17:06.684 --> 17:08.912
I'm already at it. Just sit tight.

228
17:08.912 --> 17:11.728
Just go easy on the water.

229
17:11.728 --> 17:14.449
Sure. I'll make it just right.

230
17:16.449 --> 17:18.316
You're pretty busy these days, huh?

231
17:18.316 --> 17:20.724
Don't even ask. I'm dying over here.

232
17:20.724 --> 17:22.728
Looks like it.

233
17:22.728 --> 17:25.656
Have you heard from CGM?

234
17:25.656 --> 17:26.656
Sorry?

235
17:26.656 --> 17:28.484
No, I guess they don't need me.

236
17:28.484 --> 17:30.883
What?

237
17:30.883 --> 17:33.249
Were you going to leave if they did?

238
17:33.249 --> 17:35.292
Well, I would've thought about it.

239
17:35.292 --> 17:37.340
It's not something you can solve by staying loyal.

240
17:37.340 --> 17:42.256
Honestly, if CGM takes over Korea, we'd all be out of work.

241
17:42.256 --> 17:45.276
We're not going down that easily. Don't worry.

242
17:45.276 --> 17:47.800
Why? Do we have something up our sleeve?

243
17:47.800 --> 17:49.268
Of course.

244
17:49.268 --> 17:52.592
So just sit tight and wait.

245
17:52.592 --> 17:56.272
Oh, I saw Team 5 booked a meeting room this morning.

246
17:56.272 --> 17:58.676
Is that related to this?

247
17:58.676 --> 18:00.383
Don't ask too many questions.

248
18:00.383 --> 18:04.532
Come on, I swear I'll keep it to myself, please.

249
18:04.532 --> 18:07.316
I'm just really anxious.

250
18:27.676 --> 18:30.080
Would you like an explanation of the menu?

251
18:30.080 --> 18:33.068
No. Please order for me.

252
18:33.068 --> 18:34.704
We'll take a look and then order.

253
18:34.704 --> 18:36.404
Okay.

254
18:38.816 --> 18:42.136
[Appetizer]

255
18:42.136 --> 18:45.396
Is there anything specific you'd like to eat?

256
18:45.396 --> 18:47.412
Don't ask me.

257
18:47.412 --> 18:49.508
Order whatever you want.

258
18:49.508 --> 18:51.949
Oh, okay.

259
18:56.048 --> 18:59.012
This is Batasiolo Barolo, 2020 vintage.

260
18:59.012 --> 19:01.020
Is this the wine you ordered?

261
19:01.020 --> 19:02.720
Yes.

262
19:14.324 --> 19:16.016
Would you like to taste it?

263
19:16.016 --> 19:17.749
I'll do it.

264
19:40.872 --> 19:42.572
It's good.

265
19:43.424 --> 19:45.149
Thank you.

266
20:01.284 --> 20:03.183
As for the wine,

267
20:03.183 --> 20:05.432
who recommended it?

268
20:05.432 --> 20:10.984
Oh, I chose one I thought would pair well, from wines I've tried before.

269
20:10.984 --> 20:12.796
You've had it before?

270
20:12.796 --> 20:14.496
Yes, ma'am.

271
20:43.300 --> 20:45.376
I heard you speak some Italian?

272
20:45.376 --> 20:47.949
Yes. I'm still learning.

273
20:50.816 --> 20:55.716
Is there a particular reason you chose this place?

274
20:56.388 --> 20:59.048
They have an excellent wine list.

275
20:59.048 --> 21:02.400
I thought any good meal should be paired with wine.

276
21:02.400 --> 21:03.716
And if we're having wine,

277
21:03.716 --> 21:07.972
I thought we should come somewhere with a good selection of Italian wines.

278
21:07.972 --> 21:09.540
And?

279
21:09.540 --> 21:12.612
I wanted something we couldn't have in Italy.

280
21:12.612 --> 21:15.904
Since you've been away from Korea for so long,

281
21:15.904 --> 21:18.872
I thought modern Korean cuisine would be better than traditional Korean food.

282
21:18.872 --> 21:20.560
That's why I chose this place.

283
21:20.560 --> 21:25.049
They serve Korean food that pairs well with good wine.

284
21:26.104 --> 21:27.296
Good.

285
21:27.296 --> 21:29.708
I'm glad you like it.

286
21:29.708 --> 21:35.204
Food reveals as much about a person

287
21:35.204 --> 21:39.364
as their clothes do.

288
21:39.364 --> 21:42.124
Have you figured out what kind of person I am?

289
21:42.124 --> 21:44.116
Either someone who's good at lying,

290
21:44.116 --> 21:46.916
or someone consumed by vanity.

291
21:48.260 --> 21:49.348
Excuse me?

292
21:49.348 --> 21:52.276
Your salary can't be much,

293
21:52.276 --> 21:55.728
and a woman who buys 30-euro clothes

294
21:55.728 --> 21:59.984
but has tasted wine like this

295
21:59.984 --> 22:04.796
has to be one of two things.

296
22:04.796 --> 22:07.672
Either you've never tasted it,

297
22:07.672 --> 22:11.264
or you're living way beyond your means.

298
22:11.264 --> 22:13.083
What do you think?

299
22:15.232 --> 22:18.883
Neither makes you very trustworthy.

300
22:25.683 --> 22:28.083
[Lee Ji Hye, Associate, Team 5]

301
22:32.224 --> 22:33.436
Yes, Ji Hye.

302
22:33.436 --> 22:35.680
Mr. Gong.

303
22:35.680 --> 22:37.132
How is it going?

304
22:37.132 --> 22:39.083
Mar...

305
22:40.712 --> 22:42.872
I think Martina is out of her mind.

306
22:42.872 --> 22:44.556
Is it that bad?

307
22:44.556 --> 22:48.316
I think she's determined to nitpick every single thing.

308
22:50.012 --> 22:52.949
How far do I have to accommodate her?

309
22:52.949 --> 22:54.484
Ji Hye,

310
22:54.484 --> 22:57.216
you know we desperately need Mantua, right?

311
22:57.216 --> 22:58.424
Yes, of course.

312
22:58.424 --> 23:00.312
Even so,

313
23:00.312 --> 23:02.444
you don't have to give her everything she wants.

314
23:02.444 --> 23:06.812
If we can't have Mantua, we'll find another way.

315
23:06.812 --> 23:11.796
We can't do business with someone who has us by the throat.

316
23:11.796 --> 23:14.383
Even if things aren't fair, you have to pretend they are.

317
23:14.383 --> 23:16.952
You have to at least pretend to consider each other.

318
23:16.952 --> 23:20.849
Without that much hypocrisy, you can't work together.

319
23:21.880 --> 23:23.956
Then...

320
23:23.956 --> 23:27.772
If she makes unreasonable demands, you don't have to accept them.

321
23:27.772 --> 23:29.984
Alright, Mr. Gong. I'll do that.

322
23:29.984 --> 23:31.400
I'll call you back later.

323
23:31.400 --> 23:33.100
Alright.

324
23:43.820 --> 23:45.749
She'll be okay, right?

325
24:05.856 --> 24:09.132
Do you need anything else when you check into the hotel?

326
24:09.132 --> 24:10.964
Why are you asking me?

327
24:10.964 --> 24:13.516
The person preparing it should know.

328
24:17.332 --> 24:19.849
I've prepared some cheese and prosciutto to go with the wine,

329
24:19.849 --> 24:22.749
along with brown melon, and had them placed in your room.

330
24:22.749 --> 24:25.596
I've also made sure there's plenty of water and towels.

331
24:25.596 --> 24:28.284
I've compiled a list of places to visit and restaurants for tomorrow

332
24:28.284 --> 24:30.640
and left it in a folder on the table.

333
24:30.640 --> 24:34.728
I was just asking if there was anything else you needed.

334
24:34.728 --> 24:37.516
Do you think that's enough?

335
24:39.568 --> 24:43.416
If you tell me what else you need, I'll prepare it.

336
24:44.020 --> 24:46.760
The current size of the Chinese market,

337
24:46.760 --> 24:49.849
the benefits we'd gain by entering China,

338
24:49.849 --> 24:53.368
and the losses we'd suffer if CGM enters China.

339
24:53.368 --> 24:55.949
What I need isn't wine or towels

340
24:55.949 --> 24:59.316
but data like that, wouldn't you say?

341
25:25.896 --> 25:27.596
Ma'am,

342
25:28.436 --> 25:32.188
I'll contact the office and prepare that data immediately.

343
25:32.188 --> 25:34.052
You should've prepared it beforehand.

344
25:34.052 --> 25:37.580
It was prepared. I just failed to bring it.

345
25:37.580 --> 25:40.116
That's exactly the problem.

346
25:40.116 --> 25:43.580
Did you think catering to my whims would be enough?

347
25:43.580 --> 25:46.316
Is this how Hongsung does business?

348
25:47.652 --> 25:49.616
Tomorrow,

349
25:49.616 --> 25:51.983
have them send someone else.

350
26:05.183 --> 26:07.416
[Lee Ji Hye, Associate, Team 5]

351
26:11.400 --> 26:12.628
Yes, Ji Hye.

352
26:12.628 --> 26:14.328
Mr. Gong.

353
26:16.380 --> 26:18.249
I'm sorry.

354
26:19.000 --> 26:20.388
What happened?

355
26:20.388 --> 26:23.408
She went back to the hotel upset.

356
26:23.408 --> 26:26.183
She told us to send someone else tomorrow.

357
26:26.183 --> 26:30.884
I did my best, but I just wasn't ready enough.

358
26:30.884 --> 26:32.868
I'm sorry, sir.

359
26:32.868 --> 26:35.368
No, you have nothing to apologize for.

360
26:35.368 --> 26:37.183
I was the one who sent you.

361
26:37.183 --> 26:39.704
If we weren't prepared enough, that's on me.

362
26:39.704 --> 26:41.300
No, it's not.

363
26:41.300 --> 26:44.548
I should've done more.

364
26:44.548 --> 26:46.216
I'm sorry, sir.

365
26:46.216 --> 26:49.716
No. You've worked hard enough today. Go home and get some rest.

366
26:49.716 --> 26:52.064
Yes, Mr. Gong.

367
26:52.064 --> 26:54.183
See you tomorrow.

368
27:02.716 --> 27:06.183
Doesn't this mean it's all over?

369
27:08.716 --> 27:11.340
[Choi Joo Hee, Assistant Manager, Team 2]

370
27:11.340 --> 27:13.520
Oh, Joo Hee, did you find out?

371
27:13.520 --> 27:16.584
Mr. Joo, it's Mantua.

372
27:16.584 --> 27:18.449
- Mantua? - Yes.

373
27:18.449 --> 27:22.800
They seem to think CGM's ultimate target is China through Korea.

374
27:22.800 --> 27:24.892
Hongsung plans to sign an exclusive deal with Mantua

375
27:24.892 --> 27:27.760
and enter China before CGM.

376
27:27.760 --> 27:29.696
So Hongsung is targeting China?

377
27:29.696 --> 27:33.596
Yes, Mantua's Head of Merchandising came to the office this morning.

378
27:33.596 --> 27:35.296
I'm sure.

379
27:49.116 --> 27:50.116
Hello.

380
27:50.116 --> 27:51.776
Mr. Sponza.

381
27:51.776 --> 27:53.144
Mr. Jung.

382
27:53.144 --> 27:55.316
I was expecting your call.

383
27:55.316 --> 27:58.552
I heard your CMO is in Korea.

384
27:58.552 --> 28:00.488
Are you worried that I might take their offer?

385
28:00.488 --> 28:01.696
You know,

386
28:01.696 --> 28:03.900
this is important to me.

387
28:03.900 --> 28:05.548
You don't need to worry.

388
28:05.548 --> 28:08.249
Not necessary to stand against CGM.

389
28:10.088 --> 28:12.680
Have you made up your mind?

390
28:12.680 --> 28:15.949
Thieves fight if they want the same thing.

391
28:16.888 --> 28:21.680
Okay, we'll consider Mantua having no interest in China.

392
28:21.680 --> 28:23.160
I'll see you soon.

393
28:23.160 --> 28:24.860
Sure.

394
28:50.552 --> 28:52.916
You seem pretty busy these days.

395
28:54.816 --> 28:57.804
Oh, a little... yes.

396
28:57.804 --> 28:59.280
You can tell?

397
28:59.280 --> 29:02.052
You notice things when you run a café.

398
29:02.052 --> 29:04.636
Whether someone's busy or free,

399
29:04.636 --> 29:08.416
whether they enjoy their work or hate it. Things like that.

400
29:08.416 --> 29:10.668
You look busy.

401
29:10.668 --> 29:14.316
Don't you dislike seeing people who look busy first thing in the morning?

402
29:14.316 --> 29:15.883
What are you talking about?

403
29:15.883 --> 29:18.883
That's why I open the café in the morning.

404
29:18.883 --> 29:22.232
People are more productive in the morning.

405
29:22.232 --> 29:24.012
"Productive."

406
29:24.012 --> 29:25.884
That's a nice way to put it.

407
29:25.884 --> 29:29.708
I thought things would slow down there,

408
29:29.708 --> 29:31.749
but you're even busier now.

409
29:32.960 --> 29:34.660
It's interesting.

410
29:35.368 --> 29:37.249
Hang in there today.

411
29:38.336 --> 29:40.036
Thanks.

412
30:01.216 --> 30:04.416
[Orenda Outlet, Paradis Mall Outlet]

413
30:04.416 --> 30:07.049
[Transfer Confirmation]

414
30:07.049 --> 30:08.683
[Shinhwa BKC, Hongsung International]

415
30:08.683 --> 30:11.016
[Completed]

416
30:11.016 --> 30:12.583
[Transfer Confirmation]

417
30:12.583 --> 30:14.649
[List of Penalty Payments by Country and Brand]

418
30:14.649 --> 30:17.316
[Need to check whether standard contracts are used]

419
30:18.883 --> 30:20.083
[Confirmation of Penalty Payment]

420
30:20.083 --> 30:22.216
[This confirmation is intended to prevent any future legal disputes...]

421
30:22.216 --> 30:24.616
[Finance Team, Cancellation penalty status uploaded]

422
30:24.616 --> 30:25.783
[List of Penalty Payments by Country and Brand]

423
30:25.783 --> 30:27.516
[Download]

424
30:28.383 --> 30:29.816
[Brand Europe, Brand Asia]

425
30:29.816 --> 30:32.516
[Payment Status]

426
30:34.716 --> 30:38.116
[Paradis Mall Outlet, 5,600,000,000 won]

427
30:40.664 --> 30:43.212
Yeah, Paradis Mall's deposit didn't come in.

428
30:43.212 --> 30:45.252
Put some pressure on them.

429
30:45.252 --> 30:48.044
Mr. Yang, Paradis Mall hasn't paid the penalty.

430
30:48.044 --> 30:49.504
I'll call them.

431
30:49.504 --> 30:50.552
Will that be okay?

432
30:50.552 --> 30:53.149
For me? Or for Paradis Mall?

433
30:54.249 --> 30:56.949
[Hongsung Punk]

434
30:56.949 --> 30:58.683
Darn it.

435
31:02.200 --> 31:04.416
- What's going... - We haven't received your payment yet.

436
31:04.416 --> 31:05.680
- Our finance team... - Please hurry it up.

437
31:05.680 --> 31:07.148
We are itching to sue.

438
31:07.148 --> 31:09.783
- If you want to sue... - Call back after you pay.

439
31:13.444 --> 31:16.352
This little punk, seriously.

440
31:16.352 --> 31:18.183
What happened with the penalty?

441
31:18.183 --> 31:21.283
They said Finance would send it.

442
31:21.283 --> 31:24.768
Tell them to hurry up. I don't want calls like this anymore.

443
31:24.768 --> 31:26.383
Yes, sir.

444
31:26.383 --> 31:29.316
Once we transfer the penalty and fax it to CGM...

445
31:29.316 --> 31:32.083
Hurry, hurry, hurry!

446
31:38.096 --> 31:39.796
Ms. Joo.

447
31:42.949 --> 31:45.716
[Transfer Confirmation]

448
31:45.716 --> 31:48.449
[Transfer Confirmation]

449
31:51.416 --> 31:54.916
[Team Leader Joo Sun Ah]

450
31:54.916 --> 31:55.916
Yes?

451
31:55.916 --> 31:58.796
I've compiled the companies that paid Hongsung's penalties.

452
31:58.796 --> 32:00.216
Good.

453
32:00.216 --> 32:01.383
Send them the new contracts.

454
32:01.383 --> 32:03.620
Okay. Congratulations, Mr. Jung.

455
32:03.620 --> 32:05.816
You're really going to hit them hard, aren't you?

456
32:06.452 --> 32:09.016
This isn't something to celebrate.

457
32:09.016 --> 32:12.049
The roles of the powerful and the powerless always change in this business.

458
32:15.520 --> 32:19.016
Place both hands and knees on the floor.

459
32:19.016 --> 32:23.816
Lift your back leg toward the ceiling and slowly extend it.

460
32:23.816 --> 32:27.412
Slide your left arm along the floor and reach it forward.

461
32:27.412 --> 32:29.472
And breathe.

462
32:29.472 --> 32:34.116
Now, from there, reach your left arm back and grab your foot.

463
32:34.116 --> 32:38.516
Stretch through the front of your thigh and look into the distance.

464
32:38.516 --> 32:40.049
Good.

465
32:40.049 --> 32:42.684
Now, press your arms firmly into the floor,

466
32:42.684 --> 32:44.916
and reach your fingertips toward the ceiling.

467
32:44.916 --> 32:46.649
That's it.

468
32:48.949 --> 32:50.080
[Secretary Choi]

469
32:50.080 --> 32:51.948
Good. Keep breathing.

470
32:51.948 --> 32:54.183
- Excuse me. I'm sorry. - It's fine.

471
32:56.528 --> 32:58.228
Yeah? What is it?

472
32:59.648 --> 33:00.816
What?

473
33:00.816 --> 33:04.649
[Kim Soon Wook, Executive Director, Belmore Department Store]

474
33:11.600 --> 33:14.300
The subscriber you are calling is not available. After the tone...

475
33:14.300 --> 33:15.868
What? He's not answering?

476
33:15.868 --> 33:17.684
What do I do?

477
33:17.684 --> 33:21.183
I'll just make one important call. Just a moment.

478
33:39.000 --> 33:40.000
Yes, Executive Director Kim.

479
33:40.000 --> 33:41.296
Hello?

480
33:41.296 --> 33:43.568
What do you think you're doing? Huh?

481
33:43.568 --> 33:44.983
Oh, it's exactly as you saw.

482
33:44.983 --> 33:48.464
We're lowering the commission to 15% for luxury brands.

483
33:48.464 --> 33:50.672
Are you kidding me? Huh?

484
33:50.672 --> 33:53.956
Didn't you break the contract with Hongsung because we'd cover the penalties?

485
33:53.956 --> 33:55.908
Turn the music off.

486
33:55.908 --> 33:58.216
You pull this right after we paid the penalties?

487
33:58.216 --> 33:59.440
Aren't you crossing the line here?

488
33:59.440 --> 34:02.340
Are you doing business here, or are you playing games?

489
34:02.340 --> 34:04.283
I said turn that music off!

490
34:07.012 --> 34:10.756
Executive Director, business is simple, as you know.

491
34:10.756 --> 34:12.502
We made the offer because we knew it'd work.

492
34:12.502 --> 34:14.784
If you don't like it, you can refuse.

493
34:14.784 --> 34:18.964
If you don't agree to the new contract, we won't cover the penalties.

494
34:18.964 --> 34:21.649
If you keep playing this way,

495
34:21.649 --> 34:22.983
it won't just be us.

496
34:22.983 --> 34:25.224
The other department stores won't stand for it either.

497
34:25.224 --> 34:26.483
Are you ready for the consequences?

498
34:26.483 --> 34:29.168
We're not doing this to every department store.

499
34:29.168 --> 34:32.808
We won't do this to stores that reached a reasonable agreement.

500
34:32.808 --> 34:36.300
We've already exceeded our store acquisition target.

501
34:36.300 --> 34:41.572
If you don't like these terms, you can sign with Hongsung again.

502
34:41.572 --> 34:43.683
Mr. Jung!

503
34:43.683 --> 34:46.783
Don't raise your voice, Mr. Kim.

504
34:46.783 --> 34:51.249
You're just an executive director. Why do you keep talking down to me?

505
34:52.460 --> 34:53.572
Mr. Kim,

506
34:53.572 --> 34:58.716
let's show each other some respect and do business, shall we?

507
34:58.716 --> 35:01.516
Take some time to consider it and get back to me.

508
35:01.516 --> 35:04.264
Oh, and take good care of yourself.

509
35:04.264 --> 35:06.788
Executives always seem to get sick after they retire.

510
35:06.788 --> 35:10.240
Some even pass away sooner than expected.

511
35:10.240 --> 35:12.128
You!

512
35:12.128 --> 35:13.876
Hey... hello?

513
35:13.876 --> 35:15.044
Hey!

514
35:47.384 --> 35:49.949
What happened with the penalties?

515
35:51.848 --> 35:53.649
We've got all of them back.

516
35:53.649 --> 35:57.983
They didn't put up much of a fight, probably thinking CGM would cover it.

517
35:59.749 --> 36:01.792
I feel like I'm getting indigestion.

518
36:01.792 --> 36:03.883
- Let's get started. - Yes, ma'am.

519
36:13.983 --> 36:15.449
Yes, Reporter Park.

520
36:15.449 --> 36:17.752
You can publish it now.

521
36:17.752 --> 36:20.183
Yes, thank you.

522
36:25.368 --> 36:29.849
The highest rental fees are based on customer traffic patterns.

523
36:33.216 --> 36:34.949
Hello.

524
36:35.836 --> 36:37.804
What?

525
36:37.804 --> 36:39.504
Okay.

526
36:43.716 --> 36:47.849
[Hongsung's Massive Counterattack, Will CGM's Expansion into Korea Fail?]

527
36:53.049 --> 36:56.649
I just heard about it myself. I'll look into it and get back to you.

528
36:56.649 --> 36:58.849
Well... Mr. Jung.

529
36:58.849 --> 37:00.983
L-Look at this...

530
37:03.016 --> 37:04.183
[CGM's Attempt to Crush Korean Firms, Who's actually getting crushed?]

531
37:04.183 --> 37:06.383
What's this?

532
37:06.383 --> 37:09.983
[Department Stores' Complicated Calculations, Hongsung or CGM?]

533
37:17.383 --> 37:18.949
Mr. Jung!

534
37:18.949 --> 37:20.249
What's going on?

535
37:20.249 --> 37:23.648
I thought Mantua wasn't going to partner with Hongsung.

536
37:23.648 --> 37:27.280
Hongsung just took over all storage units in Shenzhen.

537
37:27.280 --> 37:29.916
80% of Mantua's brands clash with ours.

538
37:29.916 --> 37:33.949
If they enter China first, everything we've been working toward is useless.

539
37:33.949 --> 37:35.849
I made it clear so many times

540
37:35.849 --> 37:39.516
that we don't need to enter the Korean market this way.

541
37:39.516 --> 37:41.849
Are you listening to me?

542
37:53.116 --> 37:57.649
[Hongsung Partners with Mantua to Enter the Chinese Market]

543
37:58.444 --> 38:01.284
Oh, why? I swear I'll keep it to myself.

544
38:01.284 --> 38:02.360
Please.

545
38:02.360 --> 38:05.483
I'm just really worried.

546
38:13.796 --> 38:15.349
The coffee's hot, right?

547
38:15.349 --> 38:18.383
- Pardon? - Put it down before you burn yourself.

548
38:19.092 --> 38:20.816
Okay.

549
38:24.668 --> 38:25.916
Huh?

550
38:25.916 --> 38:28.184
[Voice Recording]

551
38:28.184 --> 38:31.983
Are you going to unlock it, or should I call the Internal Audit?

552
38:34.949 --> 38:36.683
Unlock it.

553
38:45.472 --> 38:47.083
[Team Leader Joo, Sales Team 3] How about staying here

554
38:47.083 --> 38:50.049
and being our eyes and ears?

555
38:52.449 --> 38:53.636
Ms. Joo,

556
38:53.636 --> 38:57.183
I'll switch companies if you tell me to.

557
38:57.183 --> 38:59.983
But I can't do that.

558
39:04.076 --> 39:05.464
Actually, never mind.

559
39:05.464 --> 39:07.492
I won't even leave the company.

560
39:07.492 --> 39:09.192
Get lost.

561
39:12.716 --> 39:16.083
No, you've had a long day. Go home and get some rest.

562
39:16.083 --> 39:18.583
Yes, Mr. Gong.

563
39:19.476 --> 39:21.283
See you tomorrow.

564
39:21.283 --> 39:23.316
[Lee Ji Hye, Associate, Team 5]

565
39:30.216 --> 39:33.216
[Martina]

566
39:37.516 --> 39:39.268
Yes, Director, this is Gong Eun Tae.

567
39:39.268 --> 39:42.649
I'll be in the office tomorrow. Please prepare the contract.

568
39:44.249 --> 39:45.932
You're signing the contract?

569
39:45.932 --> 39:47.708
Your employee was impressive.

570
39:47.708 --> 39:50.283
She has great taste in clothes and food.

571
39:50.283 --> 39:52.644
Not that taste is what matters most.

572
39:52.644 --> 39:54.449
There was just one thing.

573
39:54.449 --> 39:58.456
I wanted to see if she could make a bad thing sound good.

574
39:58.456 --> 40:01.916
Tomorrow, have them send someone else.

575
40:04.876 --> 40:09.349
While we can't know Mantua's exact figures,

576
40:09.349 --> 40:11.449
we estimate Mantua

577
40:11.449 --> 40:15.168
would lose 12% of its sales if CGM enters China.

578
40:15.168 --> 40:18.768
We estimate East Asian retailers account for about that much.

579
40:18.768 --> 40:24.516
Mr. Gong believe we could capture over 5% of the imported apparel market.

580
40:24.516 --> 40:28.552
I'll have the requested materials sent to your hotel within 30 minutes.

581
40:28.552 --> 40:32.783
And I'll arrange for someone else to come tomorrow.

582
40:32.783 --> 40:34.916
Will someone else

583
40:34.916 --> 40:37.296
be better than you?

584
40:37.296 --> 40:40.196
To be honest,

585
40:40.196 --> 40:44.983
even if our team leader shows up, I don't think it'll make much difference.

586
40:46.316 --> 40:48.883
Mr. Gong said it himself.

587
40:48.883 --> 40:54.116
You can't do business with someone who thinks they have you by the throat.

588
40:55.536 --> 40:57.512
We need Mantua.

589
40:57.512 --> 40:59.324
We're desperate.

590
40:59.324 --> 41:03.108
And I'm sure Mantua needs us too.

591
41:03.108 --> 41:06.844
So please show us the respect we need to work together.

592
41:06.844 --> 41:09.416
Just as we show courtesy to you.

593
41:11.383 --> 41:13.416
I'll be going now.

594
41:26.944 --> 41:28.349
The easiest thing in the world

595
41:28.349 --> 41:32.164
is to say good things nicely and bad things harshly.

596
41:32.164 --> 41:35.449
It's much harder to make a bad thing sound good.

597
41:35.449 --> 41:38.949
But your staff member managed to do just that.

598
41:38.949 --> 41:41.516
I think we'll work well together.

599
41:41.516 --> 41:42.516
Then

600
41:42.516 --> 41:45.116
are you heading to China with us?

601
41:46.449 --> 41:48.316
Let's talk about it tomorrow.

602
41:55.312 --> 41:56.620
Ms. Jang.

603
41:56.620 --> 41:58.016
Yes.

604
41:58.016 --> 42:00.416
Please reserve the warehouse in Shenzhen.

605
42:04.049 --> 42:05.316
Mantua?

606
42:05.316 --> 42:09.680
They seem to think CGM's ultimate target is China through Korea.

607
42:09.680 --> 42:13.416
Mantua's Head of Merchandising came to the office this morning.

608
42:13.416 --> 42:15.149
I'm sure.

609
42:20.812 --> 42:21.949
Mr. Gong,

610
42:21.949 --> 42:24.083
I heard you decided to sign the contract.

611
42:24.083 --> 42:26.149
Yes, I truly appreciate it.

612
42:26.149 --> 42:27.883
It wasn't my decision.

613
42:27.883 --> 42:29.683
Martina made this decision.

614
42:29.683 --> 42:33.216
And the reason was your employee is outstanding.

615
42:33.216 --> 42:36.183
It was your decision in the end.

616
42:36.183 --> 42:39.116
Is there anything more I can do for you?

617
42:39.116 --> 42:42.072
You may receive a call from Jung Sun Hyuk.

618
42:42.072 --> 42:45.628
And should I just tell them we're not going to sign with Hongsung?

619
42:45.628 --> 42:48.049
I'll leave it in your hand, Mr. Sponza.

620
42:48.049 --> 42:50.224
They won't change anything in the end.

621
42:50.224 --> 42:52.284
I'll handle it myself.

622
42:52.284 --> 42:54.983
Turns out the guy who came in late at night work

623
42:54.983 --> 42:57.452
was actually here to steal from me.

624
42:57.452 --> 43:01.416
I can't just let him walk away like that, can I?

625
43:02.208 --> 43:05.216
Looks like we need to put on a show.

626
43:05.216 --> 43:07.940
There is a reason why Martina is so good at acting.

627
43:07.940 --> 43:09.908
She learned from me.

628
43:09.908 --> 43:11.783
She's just Korean.

629
43:29.383 --> 43:31.716
[Yoon Seong Shik, Department Head, Armonia Department Store]

630
43:31.716 --> 43:33.716
[Baek Mi Ha, Manager, Luceine]

631
43:33.716 --> 43:35.649
[Kang In Ja, Team Leader, Lorvenzo]

632
43:35.649 --> 43:38.249
[Yang Ji Sun, Manager, Oufic]

633
43:43.580 --> 43:46.049
I like moments like this.

634
43:47.456 --> 43:49.383
Moments that make you

635
43:50.328 --> 43:53.016
reinterpret the past.

636
44:00.800 --> 44:02.688
No matter how hard things get,

637
44:02.688 --> 44:06.383
once you pull through, the past becomes a memory.

638
44:07.176 --> 44:11.949
If you don't, it becomes a memory you'd rather forget.

639
44:13.904 --> 44:17.244
The past doesn't make the present.

640
44:17.244 --> 44:20.549
The present makes the past.

641
45:44.483 --> 45:47.183
Thank you for making time for me, Executive Director.

642
45:49.183 --> 45:52.416
I was curious why you wanted to see me.

643
45:53.440 --> 45:56.664
You have a way of making people wonder about all sorts of things.

644
45:56.664 --> 45:59.749
It's not something I could say over the phone.

645
46:00.783 --> 46:02.549
What is it?

646
46:05.152 --> 46:07.300
Sir,

647
46:07.300 --> 46:10.049
are you planning to retire from Hongsung?

648
46:12.616 --> 46:14.580
What are you getting at?

649
46:14.580 --> 46:16.516
We'd like you

650
46:16.516 --> 46:19.049
to join CGM.

651
46:25.064 --> 46:26.064
In what capacity?

652
46:26.064 --> 46:29.583
Whatever position you desire, executive director, senior advisor, anything.

653
46:29.583 --> 46:30.583
What are the terms?

654
46:30.583 --> 46:33.476
We're thinking around 500,000 dollars.

655
46:33.476 --> 46:35.176
What do you say?

656
46:42.128 --> 46:46.360
Actually, I think leaving was the right move for you.

657
46:46.360 --> 46:48.544
That's just how companies work.

658
46:48.544 --> 46:51.212
Sometimes they let good people slip away.

659
46:51.212 --> 46:55.248
Goodness, I guess it just wasn't the right fit.

660
46:55.248 --> 46:56.248
Oh, come on.

661
46:56.248 --> 47:00.188
Anyway, it's nice to see someone from Hongsung doing well.

662
47:00.188 --> 47:02.416
I just have to work harder.

663
47:03.124 --> 47:04.849
By the way,

664
47:05.549 --> 47:08.816
what are your plans for CGM?

665
47:08.816 --> 47:11.316
No matter how I look at it,

666
47:11.316 --> 47:14.104
you can't make it work in Korea with these margins.

667
47:14.104 --> 47:17.168
You think the margins are too low?

668
47:17.168 --> 47:20.516
You want to secure the market first?

669
47:20.516 --> 47:21.516
Yes.

670
47:21.516 --> 47:25.840
I want to establish ourselves early, even if we have to push a little.

671
47:25.840 --> 47:29.404
Come on, there must be more to it, huh?

672
47:29.404 --> 47:32.783
We're going to be working together now. Can't you tell me?

673
47:34.264 --> 47:35.328
Sir.

674
47:37.616 --> 47:40.116
Are you really joining CGM?

675
47:41.468 --> 47:43.772
Well, I told you I am.

676
47:43.772 --> 47:45.472
Sir.

677
47:48.620 --> 47:49.683
Was it that obvious?

678
47:49.683 --> 47:50.683
Very.

679
47:50.683 --> 47:53.016
Jeez.

680
47:53.732 --> 47:56.516
Acting isn't as easy as it looks.

681
47:57.416 --> 48:00.092
Actors deserve every penny they make.

682
48:00.092 --> 48:03.983
Alright, my treat. Let's just have a drink.

683
48:13.716 --> 48:15.404
Then,

684
48:15.404 --> 48:19.883
assuming you're not coming, let me ask you one thing.

685
48:21.349 --> 48:23.816
Why do you want to stay with Hongsung?

686
48:25.080 --> 48:27.620
You had it wrong from the start.

687
48:27.620 --> 48:29.320
What did I get wrong?

688
48:30.568 --> 48:33.449
I've been with Hongsung for 30 years.

689
48:33.449 --> 48:37.056
I've been with the CEO since he started the company in that office

690
48:37.056 --> 48:39.883
above the Gwanghui-dong supermarket.

691
48:39.883 --> 48:44.216
Do you really think I'd leave now for money?

692
48:44.216 --> 48:48.549
Then what should I have offered?

693
48:49.249 --> 48:52.340
A bigger market, a grander vision,

694
48:52.340 --> 48:54.744
something like greater prestige.

695
48:54.744 --> 48:57.683
You should've approached me with those.

696
48:59.092 --> 49:01.549
Would you join, then?

697
49:04.116 --> 49:08.148
No. I still wouldn't.

698
49:08.148 --> 49:10.183
You're the same, aren't you?

699
49:11.308 --> 49:13.916
You don't work just for money.

700
49:16.716 --> 49:19.484
If you're that kind of person,

701
49:19.484 --> 49:23.349
why did you think I wasn't?

702
50:02.940 --> 50:05.649
So, you're saying you need to keep secrets from me as well?

703
50:05.649 --> 50:07.368
If I were Jung Sun Hyuk,

704
50:07.368 --> 50:11.583
I figured you'd be the first person I'd approach, sir.

705
50:12.212 --> 50:15.616
Anyway, Ms. Park is sharp as a tack.
